# ENVIRONMENT CHANGE DURING THIS RUN, recorded for timing, NOT as a remedy.
# At 20:08 UTC the integration lead stopped the retired `foes` preview environment
# (`presidium-dev --env foes stop`, exit 0), after its owning slice was released. Its
# backend-data, cache, dependency and tool volumes and its source and artifact directories were
# retained. The shared `main`, `characters`, `foes-library` and `ui` environments were left up.
#
# So the sample above, taken at 20:04:05, covers five concurrent environments, and the remainder
# of the suite ran with four. This is a capacity change that happened mid-run. It is recorded so
# that anyone reading the results knows the conditions were not constant across the run. It is
# NOT evidence that it fixed, caused or affected any timeout, and no such claim is made.
#
# Checked rather than assumed, from the mtimes of
# /srv/dev/salient/characters/artifacts/browser-final/*/error-context.md, which Playwright writes
# when a test fails:
#
#   20:03:19  closeout.spec.ts:21        OK button in startCombat       before the stop
#   20:04:09  combat.spec.ts:31          Take turn                      before the stop
#   20:06:02  table-audit.spec.ts:40     Campaigns heading at register  before the stop
#   20:07:12  v21-campaign.spec.ts:23    Campaigns heading at register  before the stop
#   20:20:30  wizard.spec.ts:23          Take turn                      AFTER the stop
#
# So the run's failures span the capacity change: four before it and one twelve minutes after it.
# That is the whole of what the timing shows. It does not establish that the stop made no
# difference, and it does not establish that it made one; a single post-stop failure is not a
# measurement of anything. It is recorded so nobody reads this run as having been taken under
# constant conditions.
